; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5559    \REASON The passed PDU will always match a configured PDU if DET checks are active (which is mandatory for SafeBSW), and if only one Rx or Tx PDU is configured (which is a common diagnostic use case).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5560  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5561  \ID COV_CANTP_PDU_REF
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5562    \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5563    \ACCEPT TX tx tx
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5564    \ACCEPT XF tf xf
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5565    \ACCEPT XF xf xx
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5566    \REASON The reference from RxPdu to RxSdu usually always exists, so the related check will never fail in some configurations. However, specific configurations exists where this is tested nevertheless.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5567  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5568  \ID COV_CANTP_INVALID_TXCONFPDU
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5569    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5570    \REASON In some configurations, the received TxConfPdu will always match the configured TxConfPdu here, because validity is already ensured by previous checks. This happens especially when only on Sdus per direction is configured.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5571  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5572  \ID COV_CANTP_SILENT_RUNTIME_CHECK
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5573    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5574    \REASON The check is used to verify the validity of the generated configuration data. This check can only fail with an erroneous generator.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5575  COV_JUSTIFICATION_END */
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5576  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5577  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5578  /* Silent BSW Justification                                                                                           */
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5579  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5580  /* Naming Convention:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5581   * ID_SBSW_CANTP_<function>_CALL_<parameter>: justification for a call to <function> with a specific <parameter>.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5582   * ID_SBSW_CANTP_<function>_WRITE_<object>:   justification for write access to any <object> within <function>
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5583   *
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5584   * <function> may also refer to "internal", which can be any an static CanTp function, or to a feature / functionality.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5585   */
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5586  /* SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5587  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5588  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5589    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpRxState pointer is used in an internal function for write access. It is passed to this function
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5590                    as a parameter and expected to valid. Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5591    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5592  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5593  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_CALL_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5594    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpRxState pointer is used in an internal function as parameter to another function. It is passed to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5595                    this function as a parameter and expected to valid. Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5596    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5597  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5598  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5599    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpTxState pointer is in an internal function for write access and/or as parameter to another
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5600                    function. It passed to this function as a parameter and expected to valid.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5601                    Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5602    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5603  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5604  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_CALL_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5605    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpTxState pointer is used in an internal function as parameter to another function. It is passed to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5606                    this function as a parameter and expected to valid. Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5607    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5608  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5609  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_CALCBS
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5610    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_CalcBS array, indexed by the RxHdl. RxHdl is part of the struct referenced
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5611                    by the pTpRxState pointer, which is a function parameter here and expected to refer to a valid and
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5612                    initialized channel state. This implies that RxHdl is < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls, which is mapped to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5613                    CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5614                    The CanTp_CalcBS array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_RxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5615    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5616  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5617  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5618    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionRx, the pTpRxState pointer is used for write access. It is initialized to the RxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5619                    array, indexed by lRxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0 and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels-1).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5620                    CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxState in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5621    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5622  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5623  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_CALL_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5624    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionRx, the pTpRxState pointer is used as function parameter to other internal functions.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5625                    The pointer is initialized before (see [SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_RXSTATE]), and it is ensured that the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5626                    state is initialized (RxHdl != invalid).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5627    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5628  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5629  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5630    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionTx, the pTpTxState pointer is used for write access. It is initialized to the TxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5631                    array, indexed by lTxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0 and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels-1).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5632                    CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxState in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5633    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5634  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5635  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_CALL_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5636    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionTx, the pTpTxState pointer is used as function parameter to other internal functions.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5637                    The pointer is initialized before (see [SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_TXSTATE]), and it is ensured that the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5638                    state is initialized (TxHdl != invalid).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5639    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5640  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5641  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_WRITE_DEST
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5642    \DESCRIPTION    The pointer pDest and the upper limit for the used index (Count) are parameters of the function and expected
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5643                    to be valid and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5644    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5645  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5646  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_PAYLOAD
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5647    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy the payload of a received frame to the RxState struct.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5648                    The parameters Dest and Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5649                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the Payload array of the RxState struct. The array
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5650                      size is CANTP_MAX_PAYLOAD_LENGTH, which is generated. For the validity of pTpRxState, see
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5651                      [SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_RXSTATE]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5652                    - Count parameter pTpRxState->PayloadLength is set in different sections of the code but can never be
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5653                      larger than CanTp_RxCfg_GetMaxPayload.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5654    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXMAXPAYLOADLENGTH]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5655  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5656  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_FCDATA
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5657    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy a flow control frame to the TxState struct. The parameters
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5658                    pDest and Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5659                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the FCData array of the TxState struct. The array size
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5660                      is 4. For validity of TxState pointer, see [SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_TXSTATE].
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5661                    - Count parameter is calculated as CANTP_PCI_LENGTH_FC + lAddressingOffset, where CANTP_PCI_LENGTH_FC
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5662                      is 3 and Addressing Offset can only be 1 or 0.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5663    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5664  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5665  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXQUEUE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5666    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy a CanTp frame to the TxQueue. The parameters pDest and
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5667                    Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5668                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the SduData array of the CanTp_TxQueueEntryType. The
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5669                      array size is CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5670                    - Count parameter is derived from the PaddingLength and SduLength values, which are passed to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5671                      CanTp_CanIfTransmit and are expected to be consistent with the SduDataPtr. The largest array which
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5672                      is referenced by SduDataPtr (see [SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR]) has a size of
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5673                      CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5674    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5675  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5676  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXFRAMEDATA
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5677    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy from CanTp_TxTransmitFrame. The content of parameters pDest and Count must be valid
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5678                    and consistent. The consistency is also needed at other code locations and is justified with
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5679                    [SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR].
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5680    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5681  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5682  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXINIT_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5683    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_TxSemaphores array. The index is read by CanTp_RxCfg_GetTxFcConfPduId(RxHdl).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5684                    RxHdl is part of the struct referenced by the pTpRxState pointer, which is expected to refer to a valid
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5685                    Rx state.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5686                    The write access only occurs for flow controls, i.e. the TA-Type of the connection must be 'physical'
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5687                    The value read from the configuration must always be < CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5688    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXCFG_TXFCCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5689  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5690  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXINIT_WRITE_CHANNELMAP
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5691    \DESCRIPTION    With dynamic channel assignment, the RxHdl from the Rx state struct is used as index for CanTp_RxChannelMap.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5692                    CanTp_RxInit expects the state struct pointer to be valid and initialized, which implies that RxHdl
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5693                    is < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5694                    Since CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h, the CanTp_RxChannelMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5695                    array must have the same size as CanTp_RxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5696    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5697  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5698  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXINIT_CALL_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5699    \DESCRIPTION    pTpRxState is used as function parameter to CanTp_RxInit in order to reset the connection. The pointer is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5700                    retrieved by CanTp_RxGetActiveChannelPtr and checked to be not NULL.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5701                    The handle parameter to get the channel must be valid. It is retrieved via the CanTp_RxSduSnv2Hdl
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5702                    indirection table (macro CanTp_RxGetSduHdlBySduId). The range and the availability (in case of post
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5703                    build) of CanTpRxSduId is verified by DET.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5704    \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5705  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5706  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXINIT_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5707    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_TxSemaphores array. The index is read by CanTp_TxCfg_GetTxConfPduId(TxHdl).
