; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5709                    Tx state.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5710                    The value read from the configuration must always be < CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5711    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5712  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5713  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXINIT_WRITE_CHANNELMAP
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5714    \DESCRIPTION    With dynamic channel assignment, the TxHdl from the Tx state struct is used as index for CanTp_TxChannelMap.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5715                    CanTp_TxInit expects the state struct pointer to be to be valid and initialized, which implies that TxHdl
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5716                    is < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxHdls.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5717                    Since CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxHdls is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h, the CanTp_TxChannelMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5718                    array must have the same size as CanTp_TxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5719    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5720  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5721  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXSTART_CALL_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5722    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_TxStartConnection an internal function is called, where the TpTxState parameter is retrieved
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5723                    through CanTp_TxGetFreeChannelPtr and checked to be not NULL.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5724                    The handle parameter to get the channel must be valid. It is passed to CanTp_TxStartConnection() in
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5725                    CanTp_Transmit. There it is derived from the CanTpTxSduId parameter via the CanTp_TxSduSnv2Hdl indirection
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5726                    table (macro CanTp_TxGetSduHdlBySduId) and CanTp_TxGetChannelPtr.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5727                    The range and the availability (in case of post build) of CanTpTxSduId is verified by DET.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5728    \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5729  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5730  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXSTART_WRITE_TXSTATE
