; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5773  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUE_WRITE_ENTRY
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5774    \DESCRIPTION    When using the TxQueue, accesses to the queue entries are encapsulated by macros. These macros return
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5775                    an element of the CanTp_TxQueue.Entries array, which is of the size CANTP_TX_QUEUE_SIZE.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5776                    The index used by the macros is either CanTp_TxQueue.ReadPos or CanTp_TxQueue.WritePos.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5777                    It have been verified by review that these values are either set to zero, or a bit masked upon
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5778                    modification is used to ensure that the value doesn't exceed the array size. The TxConfPduId used as index is also
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5779                    expected to be valid.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5780    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5781  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5782  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUECANCEL_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5783    \DESCRIPTION    TxConfPduId is used for write accesses to CanTp_TxSemaphores and CanTp_TxQueue. The PduId is read by
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5784                    CanTp_TxCfg_GetTxConfPduId / CanTp_RxCfg_GetTxFcConfPduId, according to the SduHdl and Direction parameters.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5785                    CanTp_TxQueueCancel expects that both parameters are valid and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5786                    For Rx N-SDUs, the semaphore is only used for flow controls, i.e. the TA-Type of the connection must be 'physical'
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5787    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5788                    \R [CM_CANTP_RXCFG_TXFCCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5789  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5790  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUCANCEL_CALL_RX
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5791    \DESCRIPTION    A Call to CanTp_TxQueueCancel expects a valid Rx or Tx handle, depending on the direction. Here the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5792                    function is called with direction = Rx, and RxHdl is part of the struct referenced by the pTpRxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5793                    pointer, which is a function parameter here and expected to refer to a valid Rx state.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5794    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5795  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5796  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUCANCEL_CALL_TX
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5797    \DESCRIPTION    A Call to CanTp_TxQueueCancel expects a valid Rx or Tx handle, depending on the direction. Here the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5798                    function is called with direction = Tx, and TxHdl is part of the struct referenced by the pTpTxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5799                    pointer, which is a function parameter here and expected to refer to a valid Rx state.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5800    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5801  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5802  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUEPROCESS_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5803    \DESCRIPTION    TxConfPduId is used for write accesses to CanTp_TxSemaphores and CanTp_TxQueue. The PduId is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5804                    passed as parameter and expected to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus, which is mapped to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5805                    CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5806                    The CanTp_TxQueue array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSemaphores.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5807    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCONFARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5808  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5809  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXTXINIT_CALL_QUEUEDHDL
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5810    \DESCRIPTION    A handle, which have been read from the TxQueue, is used to get the state pointer which is used as
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5811                    parameter for CanTp_RxInit/CanTpTxInit, depending on the queued direction.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5812                    All values, which are read from the queue, can be assumed as valid here (see analysis for
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5813                    [SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMIT_CALL_TXQUEUE] and [SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUE_WRITE_ENTRY]).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5814                    Both values (Handle and Direction) are only written to the queue in CanTp_CanIfTransmitFrame. There
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5815                    the values are passed as parameters and are expected to be correct and consistent.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5816    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5817  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5818  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXQUEUEPROCESS_CALL_RX
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5819    \DESCRIPTION    CanTp_TxQueueProcess is called by CanTpMainFunctionRx, where the TxConfPduId parameter is read by
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5820                    CanTp_RxCfg_GetTxFcConfPduId. The index is already checked before to be not invalid.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5821    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXCFG_TXFCCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5822  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5823  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5824    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to SduDataPtr, either with constant or calculated index. The pointer itself is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5825                    initialized at the beginning of CanTp_RxFrame to the local array lFCBuffer with size
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5826                    CANTP_FRAME_FC_MAX_LENGTH, which is at least 4. The max offset for write accesses to SduDataPtr
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5827                    is (SduLength + CANTP_FRAME_OFFSET_FC_STMIN). SduLength can here be 0 or 1,
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5828                    CANTP_FRAME_OFFSET_FC_STMIN is 2 --> sum is always below array size
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5829    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5830  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5831  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5832    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to SduDataPtr, either with constant or calculated index. The pointer is also used in
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5833                    different function calls.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5834                    - the pointer itself is initialized at the beginning of CanTp_TxTransmitFrame to the local array
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5835                      lTxFrameDataBuffer with size CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5836                    - the max pointer offset for write accesses and usage with MemCopy is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5837                      (PCIOffset + AddressOffset + MaxPayloadLength), which have to be less than CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5838                      --> PCIOffset depends on the frame type.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5839                      --> AddressOffset depends on the Addressing offset
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5840                      --> MaxPayloadLength is read from config by CanTp_TxCfg_GetMaxPayload
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5841                      FrameType | PCIOffset | AddressOffset | PayloadLength        ||                 Requirement
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5842                      ----------+-----------+---------------+----------------------++-----------------------------------------------
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5843                      .. SF ... | ... 1 ... | 0 (std) ..... | MaxPayloadLength ... || (MaxPayloadLength + 1) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5844                      .. SF ... | ... 1 ... | 1 (ext / mix) | MaxPayloadLength ... || (MaxPayloadLength + 2) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5845                      .. LSF... | ... 2 ... | 0 (std) ..... | MaxPayloadLength - 1 || (MaxPayloadLength + 1) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5846                      .. LSF... | ... 2 ... | 1 (ext / mix) | MaxPayloadLength - 1 || (MaxPayloadLength + 2) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5847                      .. FF.... | ... 2 ... | 0 (std) ..... | MaxPayloadLength - 1 || (MaxPayloadLength + 1) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5848                      .. FF.... | ... 2 ... | 1 (ext / mix) | MaxPayloadLength - 1 || (MaxPayloadLength + 2) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5849                      .. LFF... | ... 6 ... | 0 (std) ..... | MaxPayloadLength - 5 || (MaxPayloadLength + 1) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5850                      .. LFF... | ... 6 ... | 1 (ext / mix) | MaxPayloadLength - 5 || (MaxPayloadLength + 2) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5851                      .. CF.... | ... 1 ... | 0 (std) ..... | MaxPayloadLength ... || (MaxPayloadLength + 1) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5852                      .. CF.... | ... 1 ... | 1 (ext / mix) | MaxPayloadLength ... || (MaxPayloadLength + 2) <= CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5853    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXMAXFRAMELENGTH]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5854  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5855  \ID SBSW_CANTP_STOPSEPARATIONTIME_WRITE_TXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5856    \DESCRIPTION    The TpTxState pointer is used as function parameter and for write access. The pointer is retrieved by
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5857                    CanTp_TxGetActiveChannelPtr and checked to be not NULL.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5858                    To get a valid pointer, the handle parameter to get the channel must be valid. It is retrieved via
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5859                    the CanTp_TxSduSnv2Hdl indirection table (macro CanTp_TxGetSduHdlBySduId). The range and the availability
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5860                    (in case of post build) of CanTpTxSduId is verified by DET.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5861    \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5862  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5863  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXGETFREECHANNEL_WRITE_CHANNELMAP
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5864    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_RxChannelMap array, indexed by the RxHdl parameter. CanTp_RxGetFreechannelPtr
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5865                    expects RxHdl to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5866                    The CanTp_RxChannelMap array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_RxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5867    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5868  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5869  \ID SBSW_CANTP_RXGETFREECHANNEL_WRITE_STATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5870    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to pTpRxState pointer, which is initialized before, depending on the channel assignment:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5871                    - dynamic: pointer is set to CanTp_RxState array, indexed by lRxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5872                      and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels-1). CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5873                      in CanTp_Priv.h, so lRxChannelHdl is always in range.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5874                    - static: pointer is set to CanTp_RxState array, indexed by RxHdl parameter. RxHdl is expected to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5875                      be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5876                      The CanTp_RxState array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_RxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5877    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5878  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5879  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXGETFREECHANNEL_WRITE_CHANNELMAP
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5880    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_TxChannelMap array, indexed by the TxHdl parameter. CanTp_TxGetFreechannelPtr
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5881                    expects TxHdl to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5882                    The CanTp_TxChannelMap array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5883    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5884  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5885  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXGETFREECHANNEL_WRITE_STATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5886    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to pTpTxState pointer, which is initialized before, depending on the channel assignment:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5887                    - dynamic: pointer is set to CanTp_TxState array, indexed by lTxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5888                      and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels-1). CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxState
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5889                      in CanTp_Priv.h, so lTxChannelHdl is always in range.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5890                    - static: pointer is set to CanTp_TxState array, indexed by TxHdl parameter. TxHdl is expected to
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5891                      be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5892                      The CanTp_TxState array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSduCfg.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5893    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5894  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5895  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_TPDATAPTR
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5896    \DESCRIPTION    The TpDataPtr parameter, as well as the SduDataPtr and SduLength, which are part of the referenced
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5897                    struct, are expected to be valid and consistent. The padding length from the PduTxData pointer is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5898                    always expected to be less than or equal to the length of the buffer referenced by the SduDataPtr.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5899    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5900  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5901  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5902    \DESCRIPTION    The TxConfPduId, which is part of the struct referenced by the PduTxData pointer parameter, is used as
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5903                    array index for the CanTp_TxSemaphores and CanTp_TxQueue arrays. It is expected to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus,
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5904                    which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5905                    The CanTp_TxQueue array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSemaphores.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5906    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCONFARRAYSIZES]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5907  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5908  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_CALL_TXDATA
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5909    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_CanIfTransmitFrame for a SF, FF or CF. The following constraints given in the function
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5910                    description must be fulfilled:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5911                    - "pTpData and pTpData->SduDataPtr are valid pointers": both pointers reference local variables. -> ok
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5912                    - "pTpData->SduLength is less or equal pPduTxData->PaddingLength":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5913                      This is guaranteed by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength, which calculates the PaddingLength. -> ok
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5914                    - "pPduTxData->PaddingLength must not exceed the size of the array referenced by pTpData->SduDataPtr":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5915                      the consistency is also needed at other code locations and is justified with
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5916                      [see SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR].
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5917                    - "pPduTxData->TxConfPduId is a valid CanTp TxConfPduId (< CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus)":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5918                      TxConfPduId is read from the configuration by CanTp_TxCfg_GetTxConfPduId.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5919                    - "pPduTxData->SduHdl and pPduTxData->SduDirection must refer to a valid Rx / Tx handle": SduHdl is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5920                      set to TxHdl, which is valid in this context, and SduDirection is set to CANTP_DIR_TX accordingly.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5921    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5922  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5923  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_CALL_FCDATA
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5924    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_CanIfTransmitFrame for a flow control frame. The following constraints given in the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5925                    function description must be fulfilled:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5926                    - "pTpData and pTpData->SduDataPtr are valid pointers": both pointers reference local variables. -> ok
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5927                    - "pTpData->SduLength is less or equal pPduTxData->PaddingLength":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5928                      This is guaranteed by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength, which calculates the padding length. -> ok
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5929                    - "pPduTxData->PaddingLength must not exceed the size of the array referenced by pTpData->SduDataPtr":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5930                      SduDataPtr reference lFCBuffer, which is of size CANTP_FRAME_FC_MAX_LENGTH. This can be 4 or 8,
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5931                      depending on padding activation.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5932                      PaddingLength is calculated by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength and either equals lFCFrameData.SduLength
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5933                      (can be 3 or 4) or is 8 (padding active). -> ok
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5934                    - "pPduTxData->TxConfPduId is a valid CanTp TxConfPduId (< CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus)":
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5935                      TxConfPduId is read from the configuration tables by CanTp_RxCfg_GetTxFcConfPduId.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5936                    - "pPduTxData->SduHdl and pPduTxData->SduDirection must refer to a valid Rx / Tx handle": SduHdl is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5937                      set to RxHdl, which is valid in this context, and SduDirection is set to CANTP_DIR_RX accordingly.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5938    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXCFG_TXFCCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5939  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5940  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFRXINDICATIONCF_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5941    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to CanTp_TxSemaphores array. The index is read by CanTp_RxCfg_GetTxFcConfPduId(RxHdl).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5942                    RxHdl is a parameter and expected to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5943                    in CanTp_Priv.h and can therefore be assumed to be in range.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5944                    The write access only occurs for flow controls, i.e. the TA-Type of the connection must be 'physical'.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5945                    The value read from the configuration must always be < CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5946    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXCFG_TXFCCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5947  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5948  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFRXINDICATION_CALL_PDUINFO
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5949    \DESCRIPTION    The PduInfo pointer parameter is received from the CanIf and checked by DET to be not NULL.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5950    SduHdl is passed to CanTp_CanIfRxIndication in order process a reception. The SduHdl is derived from
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5951                    RxPduId, the frame type and the address by the function CanTp_Cfg_GetSduHdlByRxPduOnly and
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5952                    CanTp_Cfg_GetSduHdlByRxPduAddress. These function which utilizes the CSL macros to resolve the indirections
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5953                    from CanTp_RxPduMap to CanTp_RxSduCfg/CanTp_RxSduCfg:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5954                     - CanTp_GetRxSduCfgInd
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5955                     - CanTp_GetRxSduCfgIndStartIdxOfRxPduMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5956                     - CanTp_GetRxSduCfgIndEndIdxOfRxPduMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5957                     - CanTp_GetTxSduCfgInd
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5958                     - CanTp_GetTxSduCfgIndStartIdxOfRxPduMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5959                     - CanTp_GetTxSduCfgIndEndIdxOfRxPduMap
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5960                    The range and of RxPduId is verified by DET.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5961    \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5962  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5963  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFRXINDICATION_CALL_RXSTATE
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5964    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpRxState pointer is set to the RxState array through CanTp_RxGetFreeChannel / Canp_RxGetActiveChannel.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5965                    The SduHdl, which is used for this, is derived in CanTp_RxIndication from RxPduId, the frame type and the
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5966                    address by the function CanTp_Cfg_GetSduHdlByRxPduOnly and CanTp_Cfg_GetSduHdlByRxPduAddress.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  5967                    For Rx direction, these functions utilize the following CSL macros to resolve the indirections and retrieve
