; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6057                    is checked by DET that is is < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6058                    in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6059    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6060  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6061  \ID SBSW_CANTP_PDURCOPYRXDATA_CALL_PDUINFO
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6062    \DESCRIPTION    PduR_CanTpCopyRxData is called two pointer parameters.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6063                    - the PduInfo pointer refers to a local variable and is therefore valid. The PduInfoStruct contains
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6064                      also the SduDataPtr which is initialized to the payload array of the RxState struct. The max value
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6065                      of the according SduDataLength is read from config by CanTp_RxCfg_GetMaxPayload. It must be checked
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6066                      that it does not exceed the size of the Payload array (CANTP_MAX_PAYLOAD_LENGTH).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6067                      In some cases, the SduLength is set to zero and the SduDataPointer remains uninitialized. It is
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6068                      expected, as documented in the SWS, that the upper layer does not access the SduDataPtr for a copy
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6069                      request with 0 bytes.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6070                    - the buffer size pointer refers to an element of CanTp_RxState, which is valid in this context
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6071    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXMAXPAYLOADLENGTH]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6072  
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6073  \ID SBSW_CANTP_PDURCOPYTXDATA_CALL_PDUINFO
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6074    \DESCRIPTION    PduR_CanTpCopyTxData is called with three pointer parameters.
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6075                    - the PduInfo pointer refers to a local variable and is therefore valid. The PduInfoStruct contains
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6076                      also the SduDataPtr which is initialized to the payload array of the TxState struct. The max value
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6077                      of the according SduDataLength is read from config by CanTp_TxCfg_GetMaxPayload. It must be checked
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6078                      that this does not exceed the size of the Payload array (CANTP_MAX_PAYLOAD_LENGTH).
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6079                    - the retry pointer is not supported and passed as NULL (as specified by AUTOSAR)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6080                    - the available data pointer refers to a local variable
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6081    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXMAXPAYLOADLENGTH]
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6082  
