; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6127                                    its size defines the range of the general Rx handle:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6128                                    - CanTp_CalcBS           (only exists if CANTP_CONSTANT_BS == STD_ON)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6129                                    - CanTp_DynFCParameters  (only exists if CANTP_ENABLE_CHANGE_PARAM == STD_ON)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6130                                    - CanTp_RxChannelMap     (only exists if CANTP_DYN_CHANNEL_ASSIGNMENT == STD_ON)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6131                                    - CanTp_RxState          (only if CANTP_DYN_CHANNEL_ASSIGNMENT == STD_OFF)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6132  \CM CM_CANTP_TXARRAYSIZES         The size of the following RAM arrays must have at least the size of CanTp_TxSduCfg, as
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6133                                    its size defines the range of the general Tx handle:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6134                                    - CanTp_TxChannelMap     (only exists if CANTP_DYN_CHANNEL_ASSIGNMENT == STD_ON)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6135                                    - CanTp_TxState          (only if CANTP_DYN_CHANNEL_ASSIGNMENT == STD_OFF)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6136  \CM CM_CANTP_TXCONFARRAYSIZES     The size of the following RAM array must have at least the size of CanTp_TxSemaphores,
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6137                                    as its size defines the range of the general TxConf Pdu handle:
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6138                                    - CanTp_TxQueue          (only exists if CANTP_TRANSMIT_QUEUE == STD_ON)
; ..\BSW\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6139  
